<h2>01. General</h2>
<ul>
  <li>QBCC Contract</li>
  <li>In reference to Item 2, of this QBCC Schedule in the contract, it is noted that this construction will be certified as Class 1(b), therefore the Queensland Home Warranty Scheme will not be applicable. The QBCC insurance premium has not been included in the construction price</li>
  <li>Full Working Drawings</li>
  <li>Soil Test and Slab Design - builders choice</li>
  <li>Local council approval</li>
  <li>Sewerage & storm water connection to suit 6m setback</li>
  <li>Electrical mains connection single phase to suit 6m setback</li>
  <li>Energy efficiency to local authority standards</li>
  <li>Final building certification to local council approval</li>
  <li>Termite treatment to Australian standards</li>
  <li>Unless otherwise specified, the works shall be constructed in accordance with the building ACT 1975 (as amended) appendix 4 and where appropriate the AS1684-2010 timber framing code</li>
  <li>Unless otherwise specified, the proprietor is responsible to provide the house site clear of any obstructions to building including removal of long grass, shrubs, and trees where necessary</li>
  <li>Unless stated otherwise, the contract price includes provision for the house water supply to be available from an existing local authority (within one metre) prior to commencement of construction</li>
  <li>Water usage during the construction period will be at the owner's expense</li>
  <li>The contract is based on mains power already being available on site prior to construction</li>
  <li>Designed wind loading of the works to be N3 as nominated on working drawings</li>
  <li>Statutory obligations, notices, approvals and fees - the following applications, notices, approvals and/or fees are the responsibility of the proprietor. NBN connection fee for single home only</li>
  <li>Engineers soil report is provided by the builder</li>
  <li>The builder cannot guarantee the energy rating of the home until it goes through the energy rating process which is taken out prior to submitting to council for building approval. The design of the home, its orientation, climate/location, content of insulation including building material all play a major role in the energy ratings result. In a case where the final design does not meet the 6-star rating and may require additional insulation, ceiling fans, window tinting etc. To meet the standard, these will be considered as a provisional sum and have not been included in the contract price</li>
  <li>All items supplied by the owner are at their own risk and the owner indemnifies the builder against all damage and/or loss and liabilities. Any delays caused by owner supplied products may incur extensions of times (EOT's) and penalties</li>
  <li>All care will be taken to supply the products nominated in the specification or in the colour selection</li>
  <li>However, due to ongoing supply issues the builder reserves the right to substitute products and materials at their discretion. The builder will always endeavour to supply similar products or products of equal or better quality and of similar value</li>
  <li>Any variations must be in writing and signed by both parties. Approved variations are to be paid within the terms of the relevant progress claim. After signing of contracts and plans, admin costs may be charged for additional variations</li>
  <li>Any request for variations will incur an administration fee of $1,500 for structural variations and $500 for non-structural variations. The administration fee will apply irrespective of acceptance or rejection of variation by the owner</li>
  <li>Please note any changes made in Annexure A of the contract will take precedence over this standard specification document</li>
  <li>Keys will be handed over on receipt of cleared funds for final payment and all extra</li>
</ul>

