<h2>38. Handover Requirements</h2>
<p>Tekna Homes has implemented two handover inspections for the owner/s to complete. A set time and date will be arranged for these inspections and the owner/s can take as little or as much time to complete the 1st inspection. It is very important to take as much time as possible on the 1st inspection, as this will impact on our subcontractors revisiting to site and may have additional costs if not defected in the 1st inspection.</p>
<ul>
  <li>1st inspection inspects entire house to identify any defects</li>
  <li>2nd inspection checks all defects have been completed from 1st inspection</li>
</ul>

<h2>39. Turf Care and Maintenance</h2>
<p>The owner/s hereby acknowledge/s that the builder is obligated to lay turf prior to handover. Following handover, it is the responsibility of the owner and/or property manager to maintain.</p>
<ul>
  <li>I/we understand that it is recommended that turf is watered every day for the first two (2) weeks (periods of rain should not be considered substitution)</li>
  <li>The turf should be thoroughly soaked for the first two (2) weeks - during hot weather, frequent light watering is suggested until you can see the turf has rooted down</li>
  <li>I/we understand that turf tends to temporarily "die off" in places before striking permanent roots, and that this is not due to faulty product</li>
  <li>In reference to properties that are handed directly to a property manager (either by Tekna Homes or the owner) it is mandatory that the above recommendations are followed. If your property manager cannot personally commit to this, we recommend an external garden maintenance company be included in the landlord's agreement</li>
</ul>

